\cf4 ## Executive Thesis\cf3 \
\
All information-processing systems\'97biological or mechanical\'97are constrained by a fundamental physical law:\
\

\f4\i \cf5 > 
\f5\i0\b **No system can produce stable, coherent output faster than the time required to resolve interference and stabilize state under noise.**
\f3\b0 \cf3 \
\
From this law follow:\
\cf6 -\cf3  limits on cognition speed\
\cf6 -\cf3  limits on AI reliability\
\cf6 -\cf3  the necessity of external memory\
\cf6 -\cf3  the inevitability of experimentation\
\cf6 -\cf3  and the observed scaling behavior of semantic cost\
\
This document compiles these results into a single, closed framework.\
\
