\cf4 ## PART I \'97 THE FUNDAMENTAL LAW\cf3 \
\
\cf4 ## 1. The Stabilization\'96Integration Law\cf3 \
\
\cf4 ### Statement\cf3 \
\

\f4\i \cf5 > 
\f5\i0\b **No information-processing system can produce a stable, integrated output faster than the minimum time required to resolve interference and stabilize state within its physical substrate.**
\f3\b0 \cf3 \
\
This law is:\
\cf6 -\cf3  substrate-invariant\
\cf6 -\cf3  independent of intelligence\
\cf6 -\cf3  independent of architecture\
\cf6 -\cf3  enforced by thermodynamics and noise\
\
