## PART IV \'97 MICROtubules (LEANING, GROUNDED)\
\
## \cf7 8.\cf3  Microtubules as a Candidate Internal Operator\
\
Microtubules:\
- operate below synapses\
- exhibit structural regularity\
- may support \cf8 transient\cf3  stabilization\
\
They are the **only plausible biological candidate** \cf8 for\cf3  a gate-like role.\
\
### Limitation\
\
No evidence shows microtubules provide:\
- hard isolation\
- thresholded locking\
- \cf7 long\cf3 -term interference-free storage\
\
Thus:\
\
> **Microtubules may modulate cognition, but they \cf8 do\cf3  not close the gate.**\
\
The external memory thesis still holds.\
\
