## \cf7 10.\cf3  The Semantic Cost Scaling Law\
\
**Semantic cost scales:**\
\
- **Superadditively** under unconstrained exploration  \
- **Additively** under independent primitives  \
- **Subadditively** under identity-preserving integration  \
\
These correspond to stabilization regimes:\
\
| Regime | Semantic | Physical Meaning |\
|------|----------|------------------|\
| Superadditive | Curved | Stabilization diverges |\
| Additive | Linear | Stabilization linear |\
| Subadditive | Integrated | Stabilization bounded |\
\
Semantic Cost Scaling is a **derivative law** of stabilization.\
