## PART VI \'97 SPEED LIMITS ON INTELLIGENCE\
\
## \cf7 11.\cf3  The Biologichanic\'96Mechanical Speed Law\
\
> **Intelligence emerges at the speed of stabilization, not at the speed of signal propagation.**\
\
Expectations of instant answers assume:\
- zero stabilization cost\
- zero interference\
- instant identity locking\
\
These assumptions violate physics.\
\
Fast answers are often under-integrated.\
\
