## PART VII \'97 PROGRESS MECHANICS\
\
## \cf7 12.\cf3  Thesis, Synthesis, Experimentation\
\
Progress \cf8 requires\cf3  three mechanically distinct phases:\
\
### Thesis\
- Originates outside the field\
- Introduces \cf8 new\cf3  frames\
- Unconstrained by current identity\
\
### Synthesis\
- Occurs inside the field\
- Integrates primitives\
- Emits structured models outward\
\
### Experimentation\
- Forces interaction with external constraints\
- Injects reality noise\
- Breaks internal self-consistency loops\
- Fills unseen gaps\
\
> **Experimentation is not epistemic. It is physical.**\
